# HolyC formatting (`holyc-riscv --fmt`)

Treat formatting like **gofmt**: the AST formatter is canonical. Do not hand-fight style.

## Required

- After editing HolyC (`.hc` / `.HC` / `.HH` / `.hh`) under the **enforced roots**, run:
  - `make fmt` (tree), or `./holyc-riscv --fmt path/to/file.hc` (files you touched)
- Never reindent / restyle by hand to please review — change code, then fmt
- `make fmt-check` / CI must stay green (same idea as `gofmt -l`)

## Enforced roots (expand over time)

Documented in `tests/scripts/holyc_fmt_paths.sh`:

- `bootstrap/seed/`, `bootstrap/hc_repl/`
- `Kernel/**/*RV*` + `Kernel/Drv/`
- `Compiler/**/*RV*`, `Adam/*RV*` (HolyC)
- `tests/exec/cases/`, `tests/fmt/golden/`

**Not** required yet: unreformed TempleOS x86 corpus, `tests/scratch/`, `tests/fmt/cases/` (ugly golden inputs).

## Exceptions

- Intentional unformattable / non-idempotent fixtures stay on the basename denylist in `holyc_fmt_paths.sh` (e.g. `e_misc_syntax.hc`, mid-line `//` cases, `DskVirtioRV.HC` until `holyc_fmt.c` is fixed)
- Avoid huge drive-by fmt of files another agent owns in the same PR; still fmt anything **you** change

## Checks

```bash
make fmt-test    # goldens + idempotency (tests/fmt/)
make fmt         # rewrite enforced roots
make fmt-check   # fail if any enforced file differs (CI)
```
